Ladybird’s action API follows Chromium’s extension_action_api: a per-tab
value wins over the global one, getPopup() returns the popup’s full URL
(GetPopupUrl(tab_id).spec()), and an invocation error keeps the wording
Chromium’s argument checks use, since extensions compare it.
setBadgeTextColor() exists only in manifest version 3’s action, as in
Chromium, whose browser_action.json has none; Gecko’s browserAction has
it too, so an MV2 extension written for Firefox finds it missing here.

A call that names a tab the extension can’t see fails with “No tab
with id: N.”, Chromium’s kTabNotFoundError, in the same wording, since
extensions compare that error’s text when they look for a closed tab.
